This tool allows you to terminate a currently running command( the command MUST be previously executed command. ). You should use this tool when:
- You need to restart a command after updating the code;
- The user requests to stop the running command;

A JavaScript function declaration to be executed by the tool in the currently selected page.
Example without arguments: `() => {
  return document.title
}` or `async () => {
  return await fetch("example.com")
}`.
Example with arguments: `(el) => {
  return el.innerText;
}`

